#. the Library's filters, each with its count after it
#: port/frontend/shell/library.cpp:832
msgid "Favourites"
msgstr "Favorites"

#: port/frontend/shell/library.cpp:899
msgid "Press Options on a game and choose Favourite to add it here."
msgstr "Options on a game, then Favorite, puts it here."

#: port/frontend/shell/pages.cpp:1094
msgid "Cancelling and removing copied files…"
msgstr "Canceling: what it copied is removed…"

#: port/frontend/shell/pages.cpp:1099
msgid "Cancelling and restoring the previous install…"
msgstr "Canceling: what was installed before is put back…"

#: port/frontend/shell/pages.cpp:1281
msgid "Cancelled. The copied files and any earlier copy were removed. Install it again to play. Saves are kept."
msgstr "Canceled. What it copied was removed, with any earlier copy of the same title: install it again to play it. Its saves are kept."

#: port/frontend/shell/pages.cpp:1283
msgid "Cancelled. The previous install is unchanged."
msgstr "Canceled. What was installed before is as it was."

#: port/frontend/shell/settings.cpp:169
msgid "Frosted glass over each system's colours."
msgstr "Frosted glass over each side's colors."

#: port/frontend/shell/settings.cpp:627
msgid "Bicubic is sharp, Bicubic Hermite a little softer, Bilinear softest. Nearest neighbour keeps pixels square. AMD FSR 1 keeps edges clean for games below 4K, at a small GPU cost."
msgstr "Bicubic is sharp, Bicubic Hermite a little softer, Bilinear softer still; Nearest neighbor keeps pixels square. AMD FSR 1 keeps edges clean for a game drawn below 4K, for a little more work by the GPU than Bicubic."

#: port/frontend/shell/settings.cpp:709
msgid "Shows the 3DS's 3D for red and cyan glasses, with the 3D slider all the way up. Colours change with it. Applies to the next game."
msgstr "The 3DS's 3D screen as both eyes' pictures in one, red for the left and cyan for the right, to see in 3D with red and cyan glasses, as Azahar's anaglyph mode makes it, the 3D slider all the way up. Colors change with it. Applies to the next game."

#: port/frontend/shell/settings.cpp:1449
msgid "The launcher's colours, corners and background. Make your own as a JSON file in {0}/themes; the text below this page says how. Games and in-game menus don't change."
msgstr "How the launcher looks: its colors, its corners and what moves behind the menus. Every theme has the same screens and buttons. Make your own as a JSON file in {0}/themes, starting from any of these: the text under this page says how. Only the launcher changes: the in-game menus and the games stay as they are."

#: port/frontend/shell/settings.cpp:1501
msgid "The selected game's picture fills the background, blurred and dimmed. Off: just the game's colours."
msgstr "The focused game's picture fills the screen behind the menus, softened and dimmed, so moving the focus changes the whole screen. Off: the game's colors only."

#: port/frontend/shell/settings.cpp:1502
msgid "A row of filters above the list."
msgstr "All, Recently added, Favorites: a row over the list."

#: port/frontend/shell/settings.cpp:1503
msgid "Filters above the list: All, Recently added (last 30 days), Favourites, and for Wii U, Graphic packs on. Off: just Sort and Search."
msgstr "A row of filters over the Library's list: All, Recently added (the last 30 days), Favorites and, on the Wii U side, Graphic packs on, each with its count. Off: the list has every game, and Sort and Search are all it needs."

#: port/frontend/shell/shell.cpp:2036
msgid "Not a favourite"
msgstr "Not a favorite"

